          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 131983,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When do you need to use <code>dotenv</code> in your project?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">When you want to load environment variables from a <code>.env</code> file into your application</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">When your environment variables are already set in the system or platform you're working on like Mimo</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">When you want to load environment variables from a <code>.env</code> file into your application.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Your first app keeps variables only in <code>.env</code>. Your second app has them preloaded by its platform.</p><p>Which app needs <code>dotenv</code> to load its variables before you read them?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Only the first app</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Only the second app</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Both apps always need it</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick Only the first app.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5 - Copy - Copy",
            "id": 131978,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Import the correct library to enable <code>load_dotenv</code> usage.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" dotenv\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" os\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dotenv.load_dotenv()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"api_key = os.getenv(\" /><text value=\"&quot;API_KEY&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(api_key)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"13\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"12345-abcde-67890-fghij-12345\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>dotenv</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4 - Copy - Copy",
            "id": 131979,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Use the correct method to print all available environment variables.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" os\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(os.environ)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"27\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"getenv\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"(\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;API_KEY&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\")\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"environ({\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  &quot;API_KEY&quot;: &quot;12345-abcde-67890-fghij-12345&quot;,\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  &quot;SECRET_KEY&quot;: &quot;mysecretkey&quot;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  ...\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"})\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>os</code>, followed by <code>.</code>, and finally <code>environ</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Use the environment dictionary to read <code>API_KEY</code>, then print all available environment variables.</p><p>Store the dictionary in <code>variables</code>. Print the key value first and the full dictionary second.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"os\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"variables\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"os\" /><text value=\".\" /><text value=\"environ\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"variables\" /><text value=\"[\" /><text value=\"&quot;API_KEY&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"variables\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"50\" endIndex=\"59\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"77\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"getenv\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;SECRET_KEY&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"variables[&quot;API_KEY&quot;]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"12345-abcde-67890-fghij-12345\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"environ({\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  &quot;API_KEY&quot;: &quot;12345-abcde-67890-fghij-12345&quot;,\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  &quot;SECRET_KEY&quot;: &quot;mysecretkey&quot;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  ...\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"})\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>os</code>, followed by <code>environ</code>, <code>\"API_KEY\"</code>, and finally <code>variables</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4 - Copy -  - Copy - Copy",
            "id": 131980,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Ensure to set a default value in case the <code>os.environ</code> dictionary doesn't hold the one we are looking for.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" os\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"api_key = os.environ.get(\" /><text value=\"&quot;NON_EXISTENT_KEY&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;default_value&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(api_key)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"35\" /><option startIndex=\"36\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"getenv\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"default_value\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>get</code> followed by <code>\"NON_EXISTENT_KEY\"</code> and then <code>,</code>, <code>\"default_value\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Set a default value in case the <code>os.environ</code> dictionary does not contain the key you need.</p><p>Retrieve <code>NON_EXISTENT_KEY</code> safely so the program prints <code>default_value</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"import\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" os\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"api_key = os.environ.get(\" /><text value=\"&quot;NON_EXISTENT_KEY&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;default_value&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(api_key)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"21\" endIndex=\"31\" /><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"35\" /><option startIndex=\"36\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"os.getenv\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"set\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;MY_API_KEY&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;missing&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"default_value\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>os.environ</code>, followed by <code>get</code>, <code>\"NON_EXISTENT_KEY\"</code>, and finally <code>\"default_value\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 131984,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What will <code>os.getenv(\"NON_EXISTENT_KEY\", \"default\")</code> return if the environment variable does not exist?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It will return <code>\"default\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It will raise an error</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">It will return <code>None</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It will return <code>\"default\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Your environment contains <code>REGION=eu</code> but no <code>MODE</code> key.</p><p>What do <code>os.getenv(\"REGION\", \"local\")</code> and <code>os.getenv(\"MODE\", \"dev\")</code> return, in that order?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>\"eu\"</code>, then <code>\"dev\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"local\"</code>, then <code>\"dev\"</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"eu\"</code>, then <code>None</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"eu\"</code>, then <code>\"dev\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
